  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Write the must-fail-before tests for D1 (worker: two same-name parts with different bytes → today one document holds the wrong bytes) and D2 (inbound, if the go is recorded). Run them and record the failures.</step>
    <step>Fix storage naming (shared helper from `UniqueArchivePath`), D1 then D2.</step>
    <step>Selection: request identity within a save; content hash for an add; server mapping to part positions; worker selects by position.</step>
    <step>Skip rule for repeated names by byte comparison.</step>
    <step>Identity: per-name saved counts; pane marks by count; failure counter by id.</step>
    <step>Gates: affected server classes by exact name, ArchTests, BFF build 0 warnings, publish delta, CVE check; pane jest, tsc baseline (68), prod webpack, eslint on touched files.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>An Outlook save of an email with two different `image001.png`, both ticked, creates two documents, each named `image001.png`, each holding its own bytes (test reads back both).</criterion>
    <criterion>Only the second ticked: exactly one document, holding the second file's bytes.</criterion>
    <criterion>After one is saved, a re-save adding the other creates exactly one more document with the other's bytes; adding the saved one again creates nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion>The pane shows "1 of 2 files named image001.png is already saved" and keeps both tickable when one is saved; both saved → both marked saved; none saved → both unsaved.</criterion>
    <criterion>Inbound mail with two same-name attachments stores two files with their own bytes.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative: a name present once behaves exactly as before (existing tests unchanged and green); an old pane that reads only `savedAttachmentNames` behaves as before; ebilling's empty selection still selects none.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative: a retry of the same save writes the same stored names (no third file, no orphan).</criterion>
    <criterion>No new service, column, package or route; publish delta reported.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The fix needs a new Dataverse column, service, package or route; or field-mapping-r1 objects to the worker change; or a byte comparison cannot be made for an existing child.</trigger>
  </escalation>
</task>
